Subject: Cantor Process Procedure Experiment Plan

@ [plan_uuid] 31ba7503-7d5a-42ec-b61b-c8a4dd1040f5
@ [requirement_set] CPPE-001 through CPPE-040

& [SpecificationPlan] is current
  + process preserved sources through separate explosion, refinement, data, constraints, pruning, exhaustion, justification, matrix, registry, canonical, signature, and phase lock
  + stop before parser, compiler, verifier, catalogue, interpreter, or tool implementation

& [FutureExperimentPlan] is machine-form-first
  + CPPE-I01 implement candidate, schema, process, IR, receipt, catalogue, invocation, result, trace, and fault forms
  + CPPE-I02 implement strict validation, normalization, and canonical IR serialization without textual syntax
  + CPPE-I03 implement deterministic compiler from normalized procedure forms to Cantor Process IR
  + CPPE-I04 implement static verifier, effect checker, bound checker, and admission harness
  + CPPE-I05 implement in-memory catalogue and deterministic interpreter
  + CPPE-I06 implement two-process token-ring procedure and normalized replay
  + CPPE-I07 run the same pipeline over hand-authored and model-shaped candidates with negative cases
  + CPPE-I08 define a provider-neutral structured tool schema and fake model-controller transcript without live provider calls
  + CPPE-I09 audit requirements, authority separation, sensitivity, retention, residuals, and release status

& [DependencyAndStopRules] are strict
  + forms and semantics precede textual syntax
  + verifier and admission precede catalogue invocation
  + interpreter precedes any alternative backend
  + fake controller transcript precedes live model-provider integration
  + stop on ambient I/O, hidden mutable state, unbounded construct, self-admission, direct model execution, or external effect pressure

& [VerificationPlan] covers the threat surface
  + deterministic source-form and IR normalization
  + schema, type, lifecycle, bounds, effects, SOP-anchor, compiler, verifier, admission, catalogue, invocation, revocation, and replay tests
  + malformed, unknown, stale, self-authorizing, unbounded, forbidden-effect, covert-input, ring-instability, timeout, and resource-exhaustion negatives
